  "scope_id": "THREEFOLD-AMPLITUDE-20261030-001",
  "title": "One amplitude for every non-colourable cubic system",
  "subject": "Corner independence of 2-colouring counts in minimally non-2-colourable cubic triple systems, and transpose duality",
  "conclusion": "For every connected cubic triple system that is not 2-colourable, removing any line leaves the same number of colourings, and the transpose gives that number at every point. Counting an Ising weight at half the knot's angle in two orders makes each line's count the average of its points' and vice versa, so every brace has one amplitude, and trisum amplitudes depend on the gluing.",
